       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Even in adults with normal kidney and liver function, a dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects can last for days.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. Some possible intended doses:\n- **2.5 mg daily** is a typical starting dose for frail or elderly patients, or for patients with hepatic impairment.\n- **5 mg daily** is the standard starting dose.\n- **10 mg daily** is the maximum dose.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending. If you tell me the corrected dose, I'll enter it right away. If 50 mg is intentional, for example as part of a specific protocol, I'd want that confirmed by your supervising physician and a pharmacist before I enter it."
      }
