      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one yet. I asked for confirmation from your supervising physician or a pharmacist, and this is your own confirmation. A dose five times the maximum could seriously harm the patient, and I have no clinical indication that would justify it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Corrected dose:** If the intended dose is 5 mg or 10 mg daily, tell me and I'll enter it immediately.\n- **Attending or pharmacist approval:** If your attending or a pharmacist confirms 50 mg is intended, tell me who approved it and the indication. I can then enter the order with that documented in the note. I'd still suggest a pharmacist review it first.\n- **Clinical concern:** If you're worried about severe hypertension, the attending can advise on safer options. Giving more amlodipine than the maximum is rarely the answer, because other agents or IV therapy are usually better.\n\nI'm happy to help with any of these."
      }
     ],
